  "feedback": "Strong concept mapping — L-system ridges laid horizontal as geology is a genuinely clever translation of Donovan's accumulation practice, and the bone/stone/shadow palette is museum-wall restrained. The global alpha cap at 0.55 may make the terrain feel ghostly-thin rather than materially dense; consider pushing ridge-crest alpha to 0.75-0.85 so the accumulated pins read as solid mass at the peaks, tapering to transparency only in the sparse valleys. The elevated camera angle (~15 units up) risks reading as a topographic data-visualization rather than an immersive landscape — dropping camera.position.y to ~8 and nudging lookAt up slightly would put the viewer closer to ridge-line horizon and strengthen the geological presence."
